                            <comment id="17102536" author="ivandasch" created="Fri, 8 May 2020 12:33:44 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=sk0x50&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;sk0x50&quot;&gt;sk0x50&lt;/a&gt; Hi, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ivan.glukos&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ivan.glukos&quot;&gt;ivan.glukos&lt;/a&gt; said, that it is good idea to discuss this fix with you. Could you please discuss it with me in ASF Slack?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17107237" author="ivandasch" created="Thu, 14 May 2020 11:54:27 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The main reason of fail &amp;#8211; if coordinator is not an affinity node, it saves descriptor with not fully deserialized CacheConfiguration and small serialized part. Before fix if affinity node joins, coordinator send CacheConfiguration with missing CacheStore, because it obtain it not from saved binary data, but from reduced CacheConfiguration. So validation of CacheConfiguration fails on joining node and it fails. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I proposed send to joined node previously saved binary data, that is correct. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Workaround for current version same, as suggests &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=kukushal&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;kukushal&quot;&gt;kukushal&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17111679" author="slava.koptilin" created="Wed, 20 May 2020 01:58:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hello &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ivandasch&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ivandasch&quot;&gt;ivandasch&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Well, the proposed change is a compromise.&lt;br/&gt;
 On one hand, it breaks a bit the conception of splitting configurations (it seems that it is already broken). On the other hand, it &lt;b&gt;does fix&lt;/b&gt; the issue, and I think it is better to have a dirty fix than waits for an elegant solution for weeks or even though months.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So, I will merge the fix soon, and create a new improvement ticket&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17114179" author="slava.koptilin" created="Fri, 22 May 2020 15:37:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hello &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ivandasch&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ivandasch&quot;&gt;ivandasch&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fix merged into the master branch. Thank you for your efforts!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
